{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2176-02-23 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I'm Dr. Lee, one of your hospitalists. You're here today for your 16th cycle of high-dose methotrexate for your brain lymphoma. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2176-02-23 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I'm okay, just a little tired. My foot pain has been worse this week, and I’ve had some blood in my stool again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2176-02-23 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. We reviewed your recent colonoscopy—it showed mild inflammation in the rectum, but the rest of the colon looks normal. The polyps were removed, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2176-02-23 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So why am I still bleeding? I restarted the mesalamine pills like they said."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2176-02-23 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a good question. Because you’re getting methotrexate, we need to avoid anything that might slow its clearance. Oral mesalamine can interfere, so we’ve switched you to a rectal suppository form."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2176-02-23 10:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I didn’t know that. Is that why I’m still bleeding?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2176-02-23 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Partly. The flare is mild, and the suppository should help target the area without affecting your chemo. We consulted GI, and they agree with this plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2176-02-23 10:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. What about the methotrexate? I remember last time my liver enzymes went up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2176-02-23 10:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ve had mild transaminitis after past cycles. It’s expected and usually resolves. We’ll monitor your labs closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2176-02-23 10:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my foot? It’s still burning, goes up my leg. MRI was normal, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2176-02-23 10:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your spine MRI, ultrasound, and spinal tap were all negative. It’s likely neuropathic pain. We’ll keep you on gabapentin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2176-02-23 10:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I just wish we knew what was causing it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2176-02-23 10:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. It’s frustrating when we can’t find a clear cause. But gabapentin helps many patients with similar symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2176-02-23 10:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my aspirin? I usually take it daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2176-02-23 10:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve held your aspirin this admission. It can interfere with methotrexate clearance. You’ll restart it when you go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2176-02-23 10:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my mood’s been okay. I know last year was rough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2176-02-23 10:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m glad to hear that. You’re still on citalopram, and Social Work checked in. You’re denying any depression or thoughts of self-harm?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2176-02-23 10:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’m stable. Just focused on getting through treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2176-02-23 10:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. We’ll give your chemotherapy around noon. You’ll get fluids to help protect your kidneys and liver."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2176-02-23 10:49:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I feel sick afterward?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2176-02-23 10:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Some patients get mild nausea. We’ll give anti-nausea meds beforehand and have more available if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2176-02-23 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. You just finished your methotrexate infusion. Everything went smoothly. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2176-02-23 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little flushed, but no nausea yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2176-02-23 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common. We’re giving sodium acetate in your fluids to help alkalinize your urine and protect your kidneys."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2176-02-23 12:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No IV bicarbonate? I thought that’s what they usually use."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2176-02-23 12:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "There’s a national shortage, so we’re using sodium acetate instead. It works similarly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2176-02-24 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs from this morning look good. Creatinine is stable at 0.7, so your kidneys are handling the chemo well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2176-02-24 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. My foot’s still bothering me, but I guess that’s not new."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2176-02-24 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, and we don’t expect it to change quickly. We’ll keep your gabapentin going."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2176-02-24 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my liver? Any updates?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2176-02-24 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re watching it. We’ll check your levels tomorrow. Mild elevations are expected."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2176-02-24 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the methotrexate level? When will that be safe?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2176-02-24 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We start checking 24 hours after the dose. Once it drops below 0.2, you can go home. Leucovorin rescue also helps clear it safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2176-02-24 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that from last time. It helps 'rescue' the healthy cells, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2176-02-24 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. It protects your bone marrow and gut from the chemo’s effects."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2176-02-25 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Great news—your methotrexate level is now 0.19. That means you’re safe to go home tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2176-02-25 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that’s wonderful! What about my liver?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2176-02-25 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "ALT and AST are up a bit—43 and 44—but that’s mild and expected. They’ll likely return to normal in a few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2176-02-25 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my blood count? I’m always a little anemic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2176-02-25 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your hemoglobin is 11.0, which is stable. It’s due to the chemo, but not low enough to need intervention."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2176-02-25 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my potassium and phosphorus? I remember last time they were low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2176-02-25 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked—they were slightly low, so we gave replacements. Now they’re normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2176-02-25 07:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. So I can restart my aspirin when I get home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2176-02-25 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, restart it tomorrow. But stop it two days before your next chemo admission to help the methotrexate clear better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2176-02-25 07:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the mesalamine? I’ll keep using the suppository?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2176-02-25 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, use the rectal suppository at bedtime for the next two weeks. It targets the inflamed area without affecting your chemo."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2176-02-25 07:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my other meds—everything else stays the same?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2176-02-25 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue your asthma inhalers, gabapentin, citalopram, and the rest as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2176-02-26 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your discharge orders are ready. You’re doing well—clear mental status, walking independently, and labs are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2176-02-26 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m really glad. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2176-02-26 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. Just remember: restart aspirin today, stop it two days before next chemo, and use the mesalamine suppository nightly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2176-02-26 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow up with my oncologist?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2176-02-26 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and GI if the bleeding continues. Otherwise, see you in a month for cycle 17."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2176-02-26 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll be ready. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2176-02-26 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done great. Take care, and call if anything changes."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2176-02-23 10:17:00",
    "admission_end": "2176-02-26 13:50:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 50-year-old woman with primary central nervous system lymphoma, ulcerative colitis, asthma, and a history of DVT/PE was admitted for her 16th cycle of high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy. She tolerated the treatment well with only mild nausea, managed with anti-emetics. Methotrexate levels cleared appropriately, reaching below 0.2 by discharge, with no renal toxicity. Liver enzymes showed mild, expected elevation. An MRI confirmed stable lymphoma without new lesions. Due to a recent ulcerative colitis flare with hematochezia, oral mesalamine was switched to rectal suppositories to avoid interference with methotrexate excretion. Aspirin was held during admission for the same reason and was restarted at discharge. She remained emotionally stable, denied depression or suicidal ideation, and was discharged home in good condition with follow-up instructions.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Primary central nervous system lymphoma, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Ulcerative colitis, unspecified",
      "Personal history of venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Personal history of pulmonary embolism",
      "Multiple sclerosis",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Pain in limb",
      "Antineoplastic chemotherapy induced anemia",
      "Antineoplastic and immunosuppressive drugs causing adverse effects in therapeutic use",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Nonspecific elevation of levels of transaminase or lactic acid dehydrogenase [LDH]"
    ]
  }
}
